<%- include('partials/header', { pageTitle: 'Help' }) %>

  <ul class="breadcrumb">
    <li><a href="/">Dashboard</a> <span class="divider">/</span></li>
    <li class="active">Help</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>Support Notes <small>application code PAYOPS</small></h1>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="span7">
      <div class="detail-box">
        <h4>Using the held payments queue</h4>
        <p>
          The queue defaults to open items only. Use the status drop down to bring
          back closed items. The search box matches on payment reference, vendor
          name, invoice number, purchase order and hold code. The filter submits the
          page again, so any selection you have made on screen is lost when you search.
        </p>
        <p>
          Click a row to select it, double click to open it. Rows shaded red are
          flagged by the overnight ERP batch.
        </p>

        <h4>Answering a vendor call</h4>
        <p>
          Vendors ring the AP hotline asking where their payment is and almost always
          quote their own invoice number rather than our payment reference. Search the
          queue on the invoice number, open the item and read back the hold reason and
          the expected pay date. Log the call as a note against the item before you
          hang up, otherwise the next clerk takes the same call again.
        </p>
        <p>
          The hotline currently takes around <b>340 vendor status calls a week</b> and
          roughly two thirds of them are answered from this screen. This is logged as a
          known service issue &mdash; see <b>INC-0042</b> (AP inquiry call volume).
        </p>

        <h4>Working an item</h4>
        <p>
          Open the item, assign it to yourself, add a note and apply one of the
          actions. Release and Return close the item. Hold, Review and Escalate
          leave it open in the queue. Every action reloads the screen.
        </p>

        <h4>Known issues</h4>
        <ul style="margin-left:16px">
          <li>The age clock counts calendar days, not business days (INC-44192, open).</li>
          <li>The clerk column is blank for items keyed by the batch user.</li>
          <li>Printing from the queue only prints the current page of 25 rows.</li>
          <li>Back button after a Release shows a stale screen &mdash; refresh the queue.</li>
          <li>Vendor inquiry call volume, no self service for vendors (INC-0042, open).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="span4">
      <div class="detail-box">
        <h4>Interfaces</h4>
        <table class="field-table">
          <tr><th>Status by reference</th><td><code>/api/payment-status?ref=</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Status by invoice</th><td><code>/api/payment-status?invoice=</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Payment risk score</th><td><code>/api/risk-score?ref=</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>ERP extract</th><td><code>/api/exceptions.xml</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Feed user</th><td><code><%= feedUser %></code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Mail relay</th><td><code><%= smtpHost %></code></td></tr>
        </table>
        <p class="muted">
          The ERP extract is polled every 15 minutes. If the poll fails the
          overnight payables reconciliation will break &mdash; call the service desk
          on ext 4471 and ask for the finance applications on call.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="detail-box">
        <h4>Contacts</h4>
        <table class="field-table">
          <tr><th>Application</th><td>Finance Systems Team</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Email</th><td>finance-apps@meridiancorp.example</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Service desk</th><td>ext 4471</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Business owner</th><td>Accounts Payable, 3rd floor</td></tr>
          <tr><th>AP hotline</th><td>ext 4400 (vendor inquiries)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Procedure</th><td>AP-114 (held payment handling)</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

